WEBVTT

01:37.720 --> 01:42.920
WEIYANG PUBLIC
SECURITY BUREAU NANSHAN BRANCH

01:43.000 --> 01:45.160
ARCHIVE REGISTRY

01:47.080 --> 01:49.680
Here it is. Yuanlongli, June 30th case,

01:49.760 --> 01:50.840
C2643.

02:05.920 --> 02:07.960
ARCHIVES ROOM

02:11.440 --> 02:13.320
Mr. Xia, you've only been here a few days.

02:13.400 --> 02:15.000
How are you so familiar with this place?

02:15.080 --> 02:16.240
Only a few days?

02:17.120 --> 02:19.240
I was already working here
before you even got here.

02:19.880 --> 02:22.600
Later, when you were
assigned here after graduation,

02:22.680 --> 02:24.600
I was transferred to the logistics office.

02:24.680 --> 02:25.520
What a coincidence.

02:25.600 --> 02:27.960
Before my dad retired,
he was in logistics too.

02:28.040 --> 02:29.400
I took over his post.

02:29.480 --> 02:31.240
I've been filling in for your family.

02:31.840 --> 02:32.680
Thank you so much.

02:33.280 --> 02:36.600
If Captain Ran hadn't kept pushing
the higher-ups

02:36.680 --> 02:39.480
for funding and gotten
this archive room built,

02:39.560 --> 02:42.120
finding all these old files

02:42.720 --> 02:44.400
wouldn't have been easy.

02:44.480 --> 02:46.920
That's right.
All the equipment here is the best.

02:47.000 --> 02:48.760
Even the system
was built with upgrade ports.

02:48.840 --> 02:50.280
It won't be outdated in a decade.

02:51.080 --> 02:52.720
Back when Captain Ran was still here,

02:52.800 --> 02:55.240
he loved spending time
in this archive room.

02:56.320 --> 02:57.760
Sometimes when I looked up,

02:57.840 --> 03:01.480
I'd almost think
he was still sitting right there,

03:01.560 --> 03:03.960
turning through files page by page.

03:29.280 --> 03:32.840
These are all the files
from the June 30th case.

03:32.920 --> 03:34.160
I won't keep disturbing you.

03:34.240 --> 03:35.280
Want something to drink?

03:35.360 --> 03:36.880
Plain water is fine. Thank you, Mr. Xia.

03:36.960 --> 03:38.720
Alright. Go ahead with it.

03:41.240 --> 03:43.720
LIST OF EVIDENCE

03:46.480 --> 03:47.680
Pattia's staff badge.

03:47.760 --> 03:48.800
MENGMENG NO.23

03:48.880 --> 03:50.000
Black robe.

03:51.480 --> 03:52.480
Cigarette butt.

03:54.000 --> 03:55.160
Letter.

03:55.240 --> 03:56.280
Herbal medicine bag.

03:58.160 --> 03:59.480
Wrench.

04:01.640 --> 04:03.400
Photo of the trunk.

04:04.000 --> 04:05.280
Blue leather heels.

04:10.240 --> 04:11.640
Where are they?

04:12.520 --> 04:14.680
Xiaohe, what's wrong?

04:15.280 --> 04:17.800
Mr. Xia, if something was added later
to the evidence box,

04:17.880 --> 04:19.240
could it have been missed in the records?

04:19.959 --> 04:21.120
Absolutely impossible.

04:21.200 --> 04:24.480
Whether evidence is stored
or someone checks it out,

04:24.560 --> 04:26.440
it must be recorded.

04:28.720 --> 04:29.560
Checked out?

04:30.480 --> 04:32.200
PHYSICAL EVIDENCE CHECKOUT LOGBOOK

04:35.680 --> 04:36.680
GLOVES

04:38.880 --> 04:40.440
PHYSICAL EVIDENCE CHECKOUT FORM

04:40.520 --> 04:42.960
YUANLONGLI JUNE 30TH
A PAIR OF BLUE LEATHER HEELS

04:43.040 --> 04:44.960
CHECKED OUT BY: RAN FANGXU
STATUS: NOT RETURNED

04:46.840 --> 04:51.000
CHECKED OUT BY: RAN FANGXU
STATUS: NOT RETURNED

04:52.440 --> 04:53.400
Xiaohe?

04:54.120 --> 04:55.040
Ms. Liang Juan.

04:55.680 --> 04:58.520
Isn't the task force on break?
Why are you here?

04:59.160 --> 05:00.400
I came to look
into the June 30th case files.

05:01.280 --> 05:02.880
The June 30th case?

05:03.400 --> 05:04.800
Wasn't that closed
more than ten years ago?

05:04.880 --> 05:05.760
What's left to investigate?

05:05.840 --> 05:06.760
I want to look

05:06.840 --> 05:08.640
into a pair of blue leather heels
from the case.

05:09.160 --> 05:10.960
Ms. Liang, do you know about that?

05:11.760 --> 05:13.280
Blue leather heels?

05:16.640 --> 05:17.680
Blue leather heels…

05:19.320 --> 05:20.160
Captain Ran asked about them before.

05:37.520 --> 05:38.480
Captain Ran.

05:39.600 --> 05:40.520
Captain Ran.

05:41.920 --> 05:43.400
What new theory are you working on now?

05:47.040 --> 05:49.760
I'm thinking about everyday things,
like food and clothing.

05:51.720 --> 05:54.480
Right, perfect timing.

05:55.080 --> 05:56.960
In your view, a pair of red leather heels

05:57.040 --> 05:58.200
or a pair of blue leather heels,

05:58.280 --> 05:59.640
which goes better with clothes?

06:00.880 --> 06:02.840
That depends on what shade
of red and blue.

06:02.920 --> 06:04.040
Mm.

06:13.640 --> 06:14.760
This cucumber is good.

06:16.160 --> 06:17.920
The red and this blue.

06:18.000 --> 06:19.280
Which would you choose?

06:20.880 --> 06:21.840
The red one is better.

06:21.920 --> 06:23.800
Right. Blue doesn't go well with pants.

06:25.840 --> 06:27.160
What if you wrapped blue leather

06:28.560 --> 06:29.880
over red shoes?

06:29.960 --> 06:31.000
Would you wear that?

06:38.920 --> 06:40.760
Wrapped blue leather over red shoes?

06:40.840 --> 06:43.840
Look, he really had
terrible straight-man taste.

06:47.400 --> 06:48.960
BLUE LEATHER HEELS

06:49.040 --> 06:52.360
Wait. I clearly remember Ran telling me

06:52.440 --> 06:53.920
those blue leather heels were lost.

06:54.000 --> 06:55.920
How were they checked out?

06:56.000 --> 06:57.920
That signature is in
Uncle Ran's handwriting.

06:58.000 --> 06:59.520
I couldn't mistake it.

06:59.600 --> 07:01.640
Maybe you weren't in good health
at that time.

07:01.720 --> 07:03.160
He didn't want you to worry more.

07:03.760 --> 07:06.080
By the way, I ran
into Ms. Liang Juan just now.

07:06.160 --> 07:08.600
She said in the winter of 2002,
Uncle Ran mentioned something about

07:08.680 --> 07:10.400
"wrapped blue leather over red shoes".

07:11.320 --> 07:12.600
Wrapped blue leather over red shoes?

07:12.680 --> 07:14.640
Maybe Uncle Ran thought

07:14.720 --> 07:16.880
those blue leather heels were fake.

07:18.280 --> 07:19.600
Fake shoes?

07:19.680 --> 07:20.720
True.

07:20.800 --> 07:22.880
There were plenty of counterfeit
leather shoes back in the 1990s.

07:23.400 --> 07:26.160
The fakest kind
were those cardboard shoes.

07:26.240 --> 07:29.040
You know, hard cardboard
covered with artificial leather.

07:30.200 --> 07:31.520
Then that explains it.

07:31.600 --> 07:35.160
Once cardboard shoes get soaked,
the outer layer peels off.

07:35.240 --> 07:37.000
Ran must've realized then

07:37.080 --> 07:38.440
that those blue leather heels were fake.

07:38.520 --> 07:40.600
But how could fake shoes

07:40.680 --> 07:42.480
be an important clue?

08:03.240 --> 08:04.360
Thank you.

08:12.320 --> 08:13.400
Welcome.

08:23.560 --> 08:25.440
Serve him a drink.

08:25.520 --> 08:27.480
-No, thanks.
-Alright, sir.

08:28.520 --> 08:32.080
Officer He, wasn't Mengmeng's case
solved ages ago?

08:32.159 --> 08:33.559
Why are you investigating it again?

08:35.919 --> 08:38.080
When Xu Meng was at Pattia,

08:38.159 --> 08:40.799
did she wear
a pair of Double Fish high heels?

08:40.880 --> 08:41.960
Blue in color.

08:42.039 --> 08:43.840
If I remember correctly,

08:43.919 --> 08:45.960
the girls working at Pattia

08:46.040 --> 08:48.120
wore uniforms custom-made by the boss

08:48.200 --> 08:49.680
from head to toe.

08:49.760 --> 08:52.360
But whether she wore them later
at the foot massage shop,

08:52.440 --> 08:53.480
I wouldn't know.

08:56.040 --> 08:57.880
In 2002,

08:57.960 --> 09:00.480
did Officer Ran ask you anything else?

09:01.080 --> 09:04.920
I remember that rainy day in 1997.

09:05.520 --> 09:06.720
FASHION BOUTIQUE

09:07.840 --> 09:09.880
Thank you. Su Yuzhi,

09:09.960 --> 09:12.400
wishing you booming business.

09:17.760 --> 09:18.600
Bye.

09:21.240 --> 09:23.960
That was the last time
I saw the handsome guy.

09:29.280 --> 09:31.640
Mr. Ran is such a pity.

09:32.920 --> 09:34.440
He was a nice guy.

09:35.040 --> 09:36.360
He was gone just like that.

09:48.440 --> 09:49.920
Hello, Ms. Lili.

09:53.360 --> 09:54.200
Officer He,

09:55.440 --> 09:57.000
it's been a long while.

09:59.200 --> 10:01.960
I'm Lili. Don't you remember me?

10:06.880 --> 10:08.720
I wasn't close to Mengmeng.

10:08.800 --> 10:11.280
I don't know anything
about what happened to her.

10:20.200 --> 10:21.600
CRIMINAL INVESTIGATION FILES

10:21.680 --> 10:22.960
BLUE LEATHER HEELS WORN BY XU MENG

10:23.040 --> 10:24.560
ON THE DAY SHE DISAPPEARED
WERE FOUND INSIDE WU SHANLONG'S HOME

10:38.640 --> 10:40.840
All arranged by color.

10:42.600 --> 10:46.080
Wu Shanlong shows signs
of obsessive behavior.

11:04.160 --> 11:05.320
In 2002,

11:05.920 --> 11:08.640
Officer Ran came to see me.

11:09.680 --> 11:12.640
I remember it was very cold that day.

11:13.520 --> 11:15.640
-Here. Have some warm water.
-Thank you.

11:15.720 --> 11:17.960
Here's our signature dish,
Spicy Stewed Mao Xue Wang.

11:20.040 --> 11:21.120
Please enjoy your meal.

11:22.280 --> 11:24.640
Officer Ran, you ordered so much food.

11:24.720 --> 11:26.560
There are only two of us.
We can't finish all this.

11:26.640 --> 11:27.800
You shouldn't have spent so much.

11:28.560 --> 11:30.280
Not at all. If we can't
finish it, we can pack it up.

11:31.560 --> 11:32.400
Thank you, Officer Ran.

11:33.680 --> 11:35.920
You're welcome. I still need your help.

11:38.480 --> 11:39.760
Can you try to recall

11:39.840 --> 11:42.200
whether Xu Meng wore
a pair of blue leather heels

11:42.280 --> 11:44.680
when working at the foot massage shop?

11:44.760 --> 11:46.600
Blue leather heels?

11:50.280 --> 11:51.440
Yes. Yes, she did.

11:51.520 --> 11:54.160
Those blue leather heels
were tall and eye-catching.

11:56.240 --> 11:57.320
You know how it was

11:57.400 --> 11:59.280
working at the foot massage shop.

11:59.360 --> 12:01.480
Everyone dressed flashy

12:02.080 --> 12:03.680
to attract customers and earn more money.

12:05.280 --> 12:07.920
Were those shoes real
or fake cardboard shoes?

12:08.520 --> 12:09.600
Definitely real.

12:09.680 --> 12:12.000
Mengmeng wasn't well-off,

12:12.080 --> 12:14.360
but she was very picky
about clothes and appearances.

12:14.440 --> 12:16.200
She would never wear fake shoes.

12:16.840 --> 12:18.720
Besides, we worked at a foot massage shop,

12:18.800 --> 12:19.960
so our shoes often got wet.

12:20.040 --> 12:22.960
If they were cardboard shoes,
they would've fallen apart long ago.

12:25.720 --> 12:27.200
How could this be?

12:29.480 --> 12:30.920
That expression.

12:31.520 --> 12:33.920
Officer Ran had that same look
you have right now.

12:39.200 --> 12:42.400
The number you've dialed
is currently on another call.

12:42.480 --> 12:43.720
Please try again later.

12:45.520 --> 12:47.760
The number you've dialed
is currently on another call.

12:47.840 --> 12:49.160
DAD

12:50.240 --> 12:51.880
The number you've dialed

12:51.960 --> 12:53.360
is currently on another call.

13:06.400 --> 13:08.240
KIDDO

13:08.840 --> 13:09.640
-Hello?
-Hello?

13:09.720 --> 13:11.240
-Who were you talking to?
-Who were you talking to?

13:12.000 --> 13:13.280
-I found something.
-I found something.

13:13.360 --> 13:15.000
-Wu Shanlong was framed.
-Wu Shanlong was framed.

13:46.040 --> 13:46.880
Are you alright?

13:51.040 --> 13:53.720
Dad, are you going to run away from home

13:53.800 --> 13:56.640
-and leave the case aside?
-Who said I'm leaving the case aside?

13:57.320 --> 13:58.160
I'm looking into it elsewhere.

14:02.440 --> 14:03.440
Where are you going?

14:05.640 --> 14:07.080
What exactly is going on?

14:09.040 --> 14:09.880
Come.

14:12.800 --> 14:13.800
Look at this.

14:15.040 --> 14:16.360
You're observant.

14:16.440 --> 14:19.440
The shoes on this rack
are arranged by color.

14:19.520 --> 14:21.840
Only this pair of blue leather heels
is in the wrong place.

14:21.920 --> 14:25.160
Whoever used fake blue leather heels
to frame Wu Shanlong

14:25.240 --> 14:27.720
must've known his daily routine
extremely well.

14:28.480 --> 14:30.520
They slipped in secretly while he was out.

14:31.120 --> 14:32.800
But after all that planning,

14:32.880 --> 14:35.120
they overlooked one thing,
Wu Shanlong's obsessive habits.

14:36.560 --> 14:38.680
Also, I thought it through carefully.

14:39.880 --> 14:41.840
The person who could frame Wu Shanlong

14:41.920 --> 14:44.240
would need to meet all four conditions.

14:44.320 --> 14:47.680
First, they held a grudge
against Xu Meng and her father

14:47.760 --> 14:49.000
or were paid to kill them.

14:49.080 --> 14:52.320
Second, they had to be able
to kill both of them

14:52.400 --> 14:53.440
and dismember the bodies.

14:53.520 --> 14:55.240
That would require
considerable physical strength…

14:55.320 --> 14:56.160
NAME LIST

14:56.240 --> 14:57.280
…and technical skills.

14:57.360 --> 15:01.720
Third, before the police
found Wu Shanlong,

15:01.800 --> 15:03.560
they already knew he had a fetish

15:03.640 --> 15:06.480
and also knew what kinds of things
he liked collecting.

15:07.200 --> 15:11.200
Fourth, they knew Yuanlongli
like the back of their hand

15:11.280 --> 15:12.920
and knew how to avoid the cameras.

15:13.000 --> 15:13.920
At the same time,

15:14.000 --> 15:16.720
they could keep track
of Wu Shanlong's movements.

15:17.240 --> 15:20.960
I went over everyone on the list.

15:21.040 --> 15:22.720
None of them fit.

15:24.200 --> 15:26.920
Dad, you went in such a big circle
and ended up back at square one.

15:27.520 --> 15:29.080
Doesn't that mean
you found nothing at all?

15:29.160 --> 15:31.080
How is that nothing?

15:31.920 --> 15:33.760
If we've gone back to square one,

15:33.840 --> 15:35.640
Ran would've gone back too.

15:36.720 --> 15:38.880
He must've hit a dead end
when he got here.

15:39.400 --> 15:40.520
Think about it.

15:41.280 --> 15:43.680
Where would he investigate next?

15:50.520 --> 15:51.720
DE-PARADOXIFICATION IN CRIMINAL CASEWORK

15:53.560 --> 15:57.040
The center is right here. Yuanlongli.

15:57.120 --> 16:00.240
EVERY EVENT HAS A CENTER
BEYOND THE CENTER, THERE ARE RIPPLES

16:04.640 --> 16:06.840
Should've said that earlier.

16:06.920 --> 16:10.920
NEW YORK BLOCK

16:11.000 --> 16:13.240
Mr. He. Mr. He.

16:18.000 --> 16:21.400
Mr. He, are you a chum salmon?

16:22.000 --> 16:24.000
What are you doing? Swimming upstream?

16:24.080 --> 16:25.320
What are you talking about?

16:25.400 --> 16:27.760
Isn't this building
a month away from demolition?

16:27.840 --> 16:28.840
You know it's being torn down,

16:28.920 --> 16:30.560
so why is a respected officer like you

16:30.640 --> 16:31.920
coming here to cause trouble?

16:32.640 --> 16:33.560
I promise I won't cause trouble.

16:33.640 --> 16:35.160
I'm just here to relive
old times for a few days.

16:35.240 --> 16:37.480
When demolition starts,
I won't hold anyone back.

16:37.560 --> 16:38.440
I'll move out on time.

16:40.280 --> 16:42.560
Mr. He. Mr. He.

16:43.400 --> 16:44.240
Mr. He…

16:50.240 --> 16:51.240
Almost there.

16:52.120 --> 16:54.280
This is Wang Wuluan's unit.

16:55.040 --> 16:58.160
In the whole building,
this is the only apartment left for rent.

17:03.840 --> 17:06.720
-Are you alright?
-I'm fine.

17:28.000 --> 17:30.200
You actually paid rent for this?

17:30.280 --> 17:31.480
There are many units here.

17:31.560 --> 17:32.920
Couldn't you just pick one?

17:33.000 --> 17:35.040
You see, you're too green.

17:39.200 --> 17:41.840
Stop. Leave that for now.

17:42.600 --> 17:45.720
Put the kettle on, make tea,
and wait for visitors.

17:57.720 --> 17:59.160
This run-down place, jeez.

18:02.800 --> 18:03.840
Coming.

18:08.200 --> 18:09.360
Officer He.

18:10.200 --> 18:11.440
-Officer He.
-Come on in.

18:11.520 --> 18:12.680
Officer He.

18:13.600 --> 18:15.600
-Officer He, you moved in.
-It's messy.

18:15.680 --> 18:17.200
-Come in.
-Hello, Officer He.

18:17.280 --> 18:19.480
There's no need to hold back
in Officer He's place.

18:20.480 --> 18:24.960
Everyone, let's welcome Officer He
to his new home.

18:26.400 --> 18:27.640
Welcome!

18:27.720 --> 18:30.720
Officer He. Officer He.
You came at the right time.

18:30.800 --> 18:33.280
It's great. We have a capable man
on our side now.

18:33.360 --> 18:35.280
Exactly. A capable helper.

18:36.560 --> 18:38.680
I came here with a mission.

18:38.760 --> 18:42.280
I need you and everyone
to help me ask around.

18:42.360 --> 18:44.960
Everything about Officer Ran

18:45.040 --> 18:47.280
in Yuanlongli during the winter of 2002.

18:47.360 --> 18:50.160
Who he met. What he did. What he said.

18:50.240 --> 18:52.040
I want all of it.

18:52.680 --> 18:55.280
Don't worry. You can count on us.

18:55.360 --> 18:56.880
-Right.
-No problem.

18:56.960 --> 18:58.160
Of course.

18:58.240 --> 19:01.000
Looks like not everyone came today.

19:01.080 --> 19:03.080
I suggest we create a group chat.

19:03.160 --> 19:04.000
-Sure.
-Right.

19:04.080 --> 19:06.920
If anyone hears anything,
post it in the group.

19:07.000 --> 19:08.560
Right.

19:08.640 --> 19:10.440
Great idea!

19:10.520 --> 19:12.840
-Right.
-Good idea.

19:12.920 --> 19:15.560
Scan the code.

19:15.640 --> 19:16.600
HE YUANHANG

19:16.680 --> 19:18.000
DAD, DON'T LET THEM FOOL YOU
ONCE YOU'RE IN, IT'S HARD TO BACK OUT

19:27.400 --> 19:28.280
-Are you in?
-Yes.

19:28.360 --> 19:30.160
-All in?
-Yes.

19:31.600 --> 19:34.320
I only notified a few of you.
Who else is coming?

19:34.400 --> 19:35.800
-Isn't this everyone?
-Yeah.

19:35.880 --> 19:36.800
No one else.

19:44.880 --> 19:45.720
Officer He,

19:46.480 --> 19:49.440
this building is run-down and creepy.

19:49.520 --> 19:52.840
Moving in here is bad for your health.

19:53.720 --> 19:55.720
What if your situation relapses?

19:55.800 --> 19:57.440
You're not my son.

19:57.520 --> 19:59.320
-You don't need to worry about my health.
-He Yuanhang,

20:00.080 --> 20:02.560
you're not a police officer now,
and you're not an owner here either.

20:02.640 --> 20:05.600
Stop causing trouble
for the Redevelopment Bureau.

20:05.680 --> 20:06.520
Jeez.

20:07.360 --> 20:10.320
Open your eyes wide and look carefully.

20:10.400 --> 20:11.160
LEASE AGREEMENT

20:11.240 --> 20:14.640
There's a signature and a stamp.

20:15.320 --> 20:16.800
I'm a legal tenant.

20:16.880 --> 20:18.840
Who's causing trouble now?

20:20.000 --> 20:22.960
Money-grubber, you played tricks
on our demolition agreement.

20:23.040 --> 20:25.280
You promised compensation
and didn't deliver.

20:25.360 --> 20:28.800
If you want to tear down my home,
that'll be at least ten million.

20:29.400 --> 20:30.840
Not one single dime less.

20:30.920 --> 20:32.320
Ten million!

20:32.400 --> 20:33.840
Ten million!

20:33.920 --> 20:35.480
Ten million!

20:35.560 --> 20:37.360
Ten million!

20:37.440 --> 20:38.680
Ten million!

20:39.600 --> 20:41.040
-We did it!
-We won!

20:41.600 --> 20:43.000
Drink some tea.

20:43.080 --> 20:44.360
Drink tea.

20:44.440 --> 20:45.680
Carry on.

20:46.200 --> 20:47.280
Is the water ready?

20:47.360 --> 20:51.440
YUANLONGLI INTERNATIONAL GARDEN

20:53.800 --> 20:55.680
-Start the chant.
-Let's go.

20:55.760 --> 20:57.760
As long as we still have our homes,

20:57.840 --> 20:59.560
we can wait!

20:59.640 --> 21:01.400
Bad terms?

21:01.480 --> 21:03.520
We're not selling!

21:03.600 --> 21:05.480
As long as we still have our homes,

21:05.560 --> 21:07.080
we can wait!

21:09.480 --> 21:13.080
Dad, can't you clean up tomorrow?

21:14.080 --> 21:16.160
The real work hasn't even started.

21:16.240 --> 21:18.000
Go home and sleep
after everything is done.

21:19.600 --> 21:21.640
Are you sure you don't need me here?

21:21.720 --> 21:23.200
We're partners this time.

21:23.280 --> 21:25.000
I manage inside. You take the outside.

21:25.080 --> 21:26.840
We'll block them from both sides.

21:26.920 --> 21:28.800
There's no way we can't crack this case.

21:29.600 --> 21:31.120
Get up. Get to work.

21:36.640 --> 21:38.240
Open the windows wider.

21:47.880 --> 21:51.520
FAKE BLUE LEATHER HEELS

22:01.040 --> 22:04.920
Dad, even the task force
can't match this setup.

22:06.120 --> 22:09.000
Before troops move, supplies go first.

22:10.080 --> 22:13.360
Team Leader He, what are your next orders?

22:13.880 --> 22:15.600
I'm not a team leader.

22:16.120 --> 22:18.160
The team leader is Ran.

22:18.240 --> 22:19.560
What we need to do now

22:19.640 --> 22:22.080
is guess what his next move would be.

22:24.360 --> 22:25.920
If I were him,

22:27.000 --> 22:30.640
once I got to Yuanlongli,
I'd first use Tremaux's algorithm.

22:33.280 --> 22:35.040
I'll do the building canvass.

22:35.120 --> 22:38.400
Tomorrow, I'll go through every place
in this building

22:38.480 --> 22:39.880
connected to the June 30th case.

22:40.800 --> 22:41.840
I'll go to the property management

22:41.920 --> 22:44.760
and check the resident
and tenant list from 2002.

22:44.840 --> 22:47.040
And ask whether Uncle Ran
visited any of them back then.

22:47.640 --> 22:49.920
Good. That's the plan.

22:50.000 --> 22:52.200
Go home now. Rest up early.

23:01.240 --> 23:02.680
How come you're older now,

23:02.760 --> 23:04.040
but still full of energy?

23:04.640 --> 23:08.040
I have more than enough strength
to handle ten men alone.

23:09.960 --> 23:11.080
Remember to take
your blood pressure medicine.

23:11.160 --> 23:13.120
The wind gets strong at night.
Remember to close the windows.

23:13.200 --> 23:16.080
You're so naggy. Go on.

24:44.320 --> 24:47.000
I'm leaving, sir.

24:49.280 --> 24:50.120
Ran,

24:52.560 --> 24:54.520
you always saw me as your mentor.

24:57.400 --> 24:59.440
But you're the one who taught me.

25:28.280 --> 25:29.640
2002 YUANLONGLI RESIDENTIAL
COMPLEX OWNER/TENANT REGISTRATION FORM

26:48.440 --> 26:50.320
My goodness! Run!

26:50.400 --> 26:51.440
Hey!

27:38.440 --> 27:41.520
Du Mingliang, can I count you as a human?

27:41.600 --> 27:44.200
Playing games all day long.

27:44.280 --> 27:46.440
I'd rather have given birth
to a bun than you.

28:36.040 --> 28:37.400
Mr. He. Bollard!

28:41.760 --> 28:45.120
Mr. He, I heard you moved in.

28:46.760 --> 28:49.360
Many people moved out.
When are you planning to move?

28:49.440 --> 28:50.600
I'm not moving.

28:50.680 --> 28:52.600
I signed a long-term lease.

28:53.200 --> 28:54.440
I spent a lot of money
renovating the shop.

28:55.040 --> 28:56.520
That money-grubber

28:56.600 --> 28:58.640
tries to tear down illegally
and not pay me a dime.

28:58.720 --> 29:01.320
That's ridiculous.
I'm fighting him to the end.

29:02.760 --> 29:03.760
Join this group chat.

29:05.360 --> 29:07.520
Holdouts Group? What's this for?

29:07.600 --> 29:08.480
We're all on the same side.

29:08.560 --> 29:10.240
Oh, so you made a group there.

29:11.720 --> 29:14.000
Mr. He, why did you move in
at a time like this?

29:14.080 --> 29:15.160
Working on a case?

29:15.800 --> 29:17.040
Let me ask you this.

29:17.120 --> 29:19.280
In the winter of 2002,

29:19.360 --> 29:20.920
did you see Officer Ran?

29:25.440 --> 29:27.560
I wasn't supposed to tell you.

29:28.280 --> 29:30.720
But now I guess I can.

29:31.880 --> 29:32.720
Go on.

29:34.200 --> 29:35.760
Come out here!

29:35.840 --> 29:38.080
If you don't give me back the mouse,

29:38.160 --> 29:39.560
I'll go on a hunger strike for a month!

29:39.640 --> 29:41.040
Oh, I'm so scared of you.

29:41.120 --> 29:42.760
A whole month of hunger strike?

29:44.360 --> 29:46.280
-Madam.
-Officer Ran,

29:46.360 --> 29:47.960
perfect timing.

29:48.040 --> 29:50.800
Help me drag this brat out.

29:50.880 --> 29:53.720
You won't let me be a cybercafe manager
or open a cybercafé.

29:53.800 --> 29:55.840
Then I'll open the window
and live on air then.

29:55.920 --> 29:57.160
Go ahead.

29:57.240 --> 29:58.760
No one's scared of you.

30:03.240 --> 30:05.200
Du Mingliang, listen to me.

30:05.280 --> 30:07.760
Whether to be a manager
or open a cybercafé,

30:07.840 --> 30:09.360
you first need technical skills.

30:09.440 --> 30:11.320
There are courses online now.

30:11.400 --> 30:14.200
You can sign up for computer science
and study at home.

30:15.240 --> 30:16.200
Where did you see that?

30:16.800 --> 30:19.160
I can register it for you.
But first, you need to eat.

30:20.960 --> 30:23.080
Come out first.

30:23.160 --> 30:24.600
Eat your dinner.

30:30.120 --> 30:31.520
Jeez.

30:32.640 --> 30:35.440
Madam, let me ask you something.

30:35.520 --> 30:39.160
Did you see any strangers
go into No. 1703 this summer?

30:39.240 --> 30:41.240
You mean the Wu family?

30:41.960 --> 30:44.880
Their door is always shut.

30:44.960 --> 30:46.800
I only saw it open once.

30:46.880 --> 30:49.280
At the time,
the whole place was full of police.

30:58.560 --> 31:02.560
Right, have you seen
double-layer leather shoes?

31:03.200 --> 31:04.240
What is that?

31:04.880 --> 31:07.560
Shoes with one layer inside
and another layer wrapped outside.

31:07.640 --> 31:09.040
Counterfeit designer shoes.

31:11.120 --> 31:12.720
I have seen

31:12.800 --> 31:14.440
cardboard shoes before.

31:14.520 --> 31:16.480
Whoever made those
double-layer leather shoes

31:17.400 --> 31:19.880
must've had something wrong up top.

31:19.960 --> 31:21.440
Why wrap another layer

31:21.520 --> 31:23.520
over a perfectly good pair of shoes?

31:24.360 --> 31:25.960
I have seen that kind of shoes.

31:26.040 --> 31:27.640
The person making shoes like that

31:27.720 --> 31:29.880
must be a very experienced craftsman.

31:30.680 --> 31:32.720
Think about it. Two layers of leather

31:32.800 --> 31:35.760
and still made to look
exactly like the real thing.

31:35.840 --> 31:38.360
You know, that's not easy.

31:38.440 --> 31:39.880
Do you know any craftsmen like this?

31:41.080 --> 31:42.120
No.

31:43.080 --> 31:46.320
But you can ask those who sell fake shoes.

31:46.400 --> 31:48.440
They would definitely know.

31:51.760 --> 31:53.600
Then Officer Ran left.

31:54.560 --> 31:56.840
Before leaving,
he specifically told me this.

31:56.920 --> 31:58.280
If I ran into you,

31:58.360 --> 32:00.920
I must not tell you that he had come by

32:01.000 --> 32:03.320
or what questions he asked.

32:04.040 --> 32:06.440
Mr. He, aren't you his mentor?

32:06.520 --> 32:07.720
Why would he hide it from you?

32:09.120 --> 32:10.320
Double-layer leather shoes.

32:12.080 --> 32:13.520
Fake shoe sellers.

32:16.080 --> 32:18.840
Right. Guess what I saw
at the night market.

32:19.360 --> 32:21.760
Those same blue leather heels
the missing woman wore

32:21.840 --> 32:23.080
are called Double Fish.

32:23.160 --> 32:25.120
Seems like a name brand. Pretty expensive.

32:26.760 --> 32:29.920
So why didn't you clear your head too?

32:30.640 --> 32:33.280
You think branded shoes sold
at the night market are real?

32:37.880 --> 32:40.440
Mr. He. You're leaving?

32:40.520 --> 32:42.600
Put the property list aside for now.

32:42.680 --> 32:44.040
Go to the Commerce Bureau.

32:44.120 --> 32:45.880
Check the list of shoe and hat vendors

32:45.960 --> 32:48.680
at the Riverside Night Market in 1997.

32:49.240 --> 32:50.680
Contact them one by one.

32:50.760 --> 32:53.240
Ask whether Ran went
looking for them back then.

32:53.320 --> 32:54.760
All vendors?

32:54.840 --> 32:56.000
Every single one.

32:56.080 --> 32:57.760
That's a huge workload.

32:57.840 --> 32:58.840
Hurry up.

32:59.640 --> 33:01.320
Give us a straight answer.

33:01.400 --> 33:03.920
Can the relocation payout
still be negotiated or not?

33:04.000 --> 33:07.000
Otherwise, we old folks here
would rather die

33:07.080 --> 33:09.400
right here in Yuanlongli.

33:09.480 --> 33:11.640
Right! We'll die right here in Yuanlongli!

33:11.720 --> 33:13.080
As long as we still have our homes,

33:13.160 --> 33:15.120
we can wait!

33:15.200 --> 33:16.840
Bad terms?

33:16.920 --> 33:18.280
We're not selling!

33:18.360 --> 33:20.280
Everyone, please calm down.

33:20.360 --> 33:22.240
Kick up all the fuss you want.

33:22.320 --> 33:24.560
Not one extra dime
will be added to the compensation.

33:24.640 --> 33:26.200
-You!
-When the time comes,

33:26.280 --> 33:28.320
I'll bring the demolition crew
and bury explosives here.

33:28.400 --> 33:29.320
Whoever won't leave,

33:29.400 --> 33:31.320
I'll bury explosives at their front door.

33:31.400 --> 33:33.800
-How can you say this?
-Qian, you bastard!

33:33.880 --> 33:34.880
If you dare do that,

33:34.960 --> 33:36.560
I'll drag you down with me!

33:36.640 --> 33:38.640
Exactly! Go down together!

33:39.360 --> 33:40.960
-Alright, everyone.
-Go down together!

33:41.040 --> 33:42.840
Will you stop already?

33:42.920 --> 33:45.680
I'm the project manager here.
You just need to cooperate.

33:45.760 --> 33:46.600
We're all old neighbors.

33:46.680 --> 33:48.320
Is there any point in bluffing
and tricking them like this?

33:49.160 --> 33:50.000
I cooperate with you?

33:50.920 --> 33:53.880
Everyone from Yuanlongli knows
what kind of person you used to be.

33:59.360 --> 34:02.400
Some people have dirty minds.

34:02.480 --> 34:03.640
So everything they see looks dirty.

34:06.000 --> 34:06.840
Officer He,

34:07.560 --> 34:09.719
this is a matter for the owners.

34:09.800 --> 34:11.679
You're just a tenant.
You don't get a share of the money, right?

34:14.040 --> 34:16.880
Qian, you're not young anymore.

34:17.679 --> 34:19.560
You should really do something
about your bad breath.

34:20.920 --> 34:22.280
Well said!

34:22.360 --> 34:24.239
Exactly right!

34:26.760 --> 34:27.880
Let me make this clear.

34:27.960 --> 34:31.560
Everyone should raise demands
reasonably and legally.

34:31.639 --> 34:33.199
Don't act without order.

34:33.880 --> 34:36.159
Qiao is only doing her job.

34:36.239 --> 34:37.760
But the way she handles things

34:37.840 --> 34:39.679
is nothing like certain people.

34:40.280 --> 34:42.719
So don't lash out at everybody.

34:42.800 --> 34:44.040
Can you do that?

34:49.400 --> 34:52.400
Can't do it? Then I'm leaving
the group chat right now.

34:53.000 --> 34:54.600
-Please!
-No!

34:54.679 --> 34:56.520
-Officer He!
-Officer He,

34:57.280 --> 34:59.680
what you just said
was deeply philosophical.

35:00.400 --> 35:03.400
From now on, we won't
make things hard for Miss Qiao.

35:03.480 --> 35:04.320
-We won't do that.
-That's right.

35:04.400 --> 35:05.200
We won't do that to her.

35:05.280 --> 35:06.400
No.

35:07.400 --> 35:09.880
We'll go after the one
who's really to blame.

35:09.960 --> 35:11.280
-That's right.
-We'll go after the one

35:11.360 --> 35:12.320
who's really to blame.

35:12.400 --> 35:14.440
As long as we still have our homes,

35:14.520 --> 35:16.280
we can wait!

35:16.360 --> 35:18.200
Bad terms?

35:18.280 --> 35:20.480
As long as we still have our homes…

35:20.560 --> 35:22.680
As long as we still have our homes,

35:22.760 --> 35:24.720
we can wait!

35:24.800 --> 35:26.600
Bad terms?

35:26.680 --> 35:28.680
We're not selling!

35:28.760 --> 35:30.880
Qiao, don't worry.

35:30.960 --> 35:33.320
As long as I'm here,
nothing will go wrong.

35:34.080 --> 35:35.640
Thank you, Mr. He.

35:36.560 --> 35:39.920
There's something I'd like
to ask for your help with.

35:41.840 --> 35:42.680
Can you think of a way

35:42.760 --> 35:45.680
to delay the demolition deadline
a little longer?

35:46.360 --> 35:47.400
Mr. He,

35:48.240 --> 35:51.000
why did you get involved in this too?

35:51.080 --> 35:53.080
Ran left with regret.

35:54.560 --> 35:57.400
I have to stay in Yuanlongli for a while

35:57.480 --> 36:00.120
and help him make up for it
and fulfill his wish.

36:08.360 --> 36:09.200
Alright.

36:10.120 --> 36:11.360
I'll do my best to help.

36:26.480 --> 36:28.440
Mister, please do me a favor.

36:28.520 --> 36:30.040
I'll remember you for life.

36:41.560 --> 36:43.600
TO LET

36:53.240 --> 36:54.200
CALL

36:57.520 --> 36:58.520
Hello?

36:58.600 --> 36:59.880
Hello?

36:59.960 --> 37:02.280
I'd like to ask about the shop
you had for rent.

37:02.360 --> 37:05.040
Did you rent it to a woman
who sold shoes in 1997?

37:05.680 --> 37:07.840
1997? I can't remember.

37:07.920 --> 37:09.880
She had short hair and was very outgoing.

37:09.960 --> 37:11.640
Whenever someone passed her shop,

37:11.720 --> 37:13.520
she'd pull them over to look at her shoes.

37:14.120 --> 37:15.560
And she would say things like,

37:16.360 --> 37:18.200
"Please do me a favor, mister.

37:18.280 --> 37:20.760
I'll remember you for life."

37:21.400 --> 37:23.880
Now I remember. That must be Liu Guifang.

37:23.960 --> 37:25.600
She couldn't afford the rent anymore.

37:25.680 --> 37:27.120
She insisted on using
her stock to cover it.

37:27.200 --> 37:28.520
Those were the exact words she used.

37:29.120 --> 37:31.160
I felt soft-hearted at the time,
so I let it slide.

37:31.240 --> 37:32.440
Where did she go after that?

37:52.560 --> 37:55.000
I called you.
Why was your phone off again?

37:55.080 --> 37:57.480
Do you know how many vendors

37:57.560 --> 37:58.880
there were at
Riverside Night Market in 1997?

37:59.480 --> 38:00.400
More than 500.

38:00.480 --> 38:02.200
Even if I had three phones,
they would all be dead by now.

38:03.760 --> 38:04.760
Did you find anything?

38:06.600 --> 38:11.120
Uncle Ran contacted
someone named Liu Guifang.

38:12.120 --> 38:13.080
Here.

38:13.160 --> 38:14.000
LIU GUIFANG

38:43.920 --> 38:45.840
MAHJONG AND TEA,WELCOME INSIDE

38:48.240 --> 38:50.960
I heard Liu Guifang got together
with the owner of a mahjong parlor.

38:51.040 --> 38:52.400
He received a hefty demolition payout

38:52.480 --> 38:54.000
from several houses
he owned in the village.

38:54.080 --> 38:55.120
He got rich long ago.

39:12.240 --> 39:14.640
Come on. Be generous.

39:14.720 --> 39:16.600
Just do me a favor, mister.

39:16.680 --> 39:18.160
I'll remember you for life.

39:22.480 --> 39:24.880
Alright. I'm hanging up now, Yao.

39:26.320 --> 39:28.520
-Excuse me.
-Playing mahjong?

39:28.600 --> 39:30.200
Five years ago,
at the Riverside Night Market,

39:30.280 --> 39:32.000
you sold me a pair of fake leather shoes.

39:32.080 --> 39:33.080
They were cardboard shoes.

39:33.160 --> 39:34.840
What? Five years ago?

39:39.080 --> 39:40.080
It's been five years.

39:40.680 --> 39:43.800
Mister, you really hold grudges.

39:45.640 --> 39:47.440
I definitely don't remember you.

39:47.520 --> 39:49.440
But back then, I did sell fake shoes.

39:50.520 --> 39:53.200
How about this?
I'll pay you ten times the price.

39:53.280 --> 39:54.520
Is that okay?

40:02.760 --> 40:04.880
You sold Double Fish back then.

40:04.960 --> 40:05.960
They came in several colors.

40:06.040 --> 40:07.080
Do you know who in Weiyang

40:07.160 --> 40:09.000
could make this kind
of double-layer leather heels?

40:09.080 --> 40:10.560
Double-layer leather heels?

40:11.160 --> 40:12.480
Let me see.

40:14.520 --> 40:15.520
Don't open it.

40:18.360 --> 40:20.520
Double-layer leather heels…
That's pretty unusual.

40:21.120 --> 40:23.440
Judging from the finish and workmanship,

40:23.520 --> 40:26.120
that should be Mr. Lu
from Pingzhao County.

40:26.960 --> 40:28.000
Bet you didn't know.

40:28.080 --> 40:30.720
Mr. Lu was a master
of fake shoes in Weiyang.

40:30.800 --> 40:32.880
The shoes he made
could pass for the real thing.

40:34.120 --> 40:35.520
Pingzhao County.

40:38.680 --> 40:39.840
MAP

40:41.880 --> 40:45.040
PINGZHAO COUNTY

40:57.120 --> 41:00.400
PINGZHAO COUNTY

41:01.160 --> 41:02.400
It's been 13 years.

41:03.200 --> 41:05.840
No idea whether Mr. Lu is still around.

41:08.000 --> 41:09.560
NO. 6, LU VILLAGE, BEISHI TOWN
PINGZHAO COUNTY, WEIYANG CITY

41:09.640 --> 41:12.360
Uncle Ran probably
has taken this road too.

41:15.560 --> 41:17.360
We've picked the trail back up at last.
